A||||5||V8Fiero||About to  give up....need some words of encouragement||||9||
Z||000000||V8Fiero||04-16-2001||10:46 PM||||Well,<P>I have been working on the V8 for over about 2 yrs now. First it was money (ok has always been the lack of money, Damn these conversions arent cheap), then lack of space to work on it.(no garage for awhile) I have driven this car for a month or so last summer.....damn it scoots....Been toying with the idea of selling and just getting a really nice fiero.......<P>I have an 85 that I drive daily.....love that car also....<P>I know that if I sold my V8 I would kick myself in the a$$ later on though...it just seems that this is turning into a money pit, that is if I wanna do it right.....<P>Heres whats left to "finish". (yea right, are they ever finished?)<P>1.Realign the water pump pulley (Archie kit)<BR>2.Wheels and tires (16" rims on the way)<BR>3.4 wheel alignment<BR>4.Sand and prep the car.<BR>5.Paint<BR>6.Interior<BR>Oh yea, it needs rear wheel bearing also.<P>As you can see most of the "hard" work is done, Im just getting impatient I suppose.....I have more time to work on it than I do money......That sucks...<P>Any wise words out there????<P>Sorry to ramble...just needed to get this off my chest <P>Peace...||||reg||9
Z||000001||Tryxalon||04-16-2001||11:04 PM||||Hang in there, V8Fiero!! <P>If it was easy, cheap, or quick everyone would do it and it wouldn't be worth much. <P>Keep your focus on the dream, man!! ||||reg||14
Z||000002||fyerstarter||04-16-2001||11:20 PM||||I hear ya dude. I love my 87 Gt to death but it is my daily driver and I have a fairly long commute to work every day. With 110,000 miles on it the motor is starting to knock and I don't know how much life she has left in her. I have no garage to work on it myself and the price to have a shop do it is beyond my budget. What really pisses me off is all the work I have put into it over the past year and just when I was planning on getting painted soon this happens.<P>Will this make you feel any better? Probably not, but hey misery loves company :P||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GTZ34||04-17-2001||12:00 AM||||V8 - Being the Fiero lover that you are, I can't imagine you'd stop after all of ups and downs of 2 years of hard work and saving money etc. without fully enjoying your completed car. (talk about ramble...)  I mean, that's like following a dream to run in a marathon, training and sacrificing,  finally running in the race up to the point of the last 1/8 mi where you can see the finish line, and then saying, "ah screw it..."  I know, doing a V8 swap is a lot harder than training & running in a marathon so maybe its not a good analogy.   My point is... you're almost there dude, stay in it and see it through to the end, throw a party, race a few stangs vettes and what not.<p>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 04-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroHarry||04-17-2001||12:06 AM||||V8, sounds to me like all the hard work is done.......... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Dont get impatient now, your almost ready to show.........<P>------------------<BR>Harry<BR>FOCOSEVA<BR>1985 GT 258K+ "TEMPTATION"||||reg||1
Z||000005||V8Fiero||04-17-2001||12:12 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Yea, I know Im close. I guess all this crappy weather we have been having here is getting me down. Snowed on Friday, melted Sat, Snowed on Sun, melted Monday. Can you blame a guy....Damn why do I live in ND?<P>Thanks for the support guys. Hopefully before fall is over I can post a pic of my freshly painted car and make some other fiero owners want to do the same to their cars.......<P>Scott||||reg||1
